<title>USA: Environmental Tectonics gets $3.2mln order.</title>
<headline>Environmental Tectonics gets $3.2mln order.</headline>
<dateline>SOUTHAMPTON, Pa. 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Environmental Tectonics Corp said Monday it won $3.2 million of new contracts, putting the company's order backlog at $43.6 million.</p>
<p>The company said an unspecified South Asian country bought more than $2 million of aircrew training systems equipment. It added it received an other $1.2 million follow-on order for aircrew training systems and sterilization equipment</p>
<p>The orders put its backlog at $43.6 million, the company said.  </p>
<p>Environmental also said the U.S. Air Force Institute of Technology in Dayton, Ohio, recently said it would extend its cooperative research and development agreement (CRADA) with the company.</p>
</text>
